    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0443" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Brigadier General Henry A.
                        Byroade, at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-13">13 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Following, your 328<anchor n="37" xml:id="d192-f1"/> refers, information
                    received from General Chang Chih Chung through Colonel Pee regarding Canton
                    area. Generalissimo has issued order to General Chang Fa Kwei to allow Executive
                    Headquarters team to proceed to disputed area. This is <pb facs="0444" n="432"
                        xml:id="pg432"/> interpreted by Pee as recognition by the National
                    Government to General Tseng Shang’s forces as Communists.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
